1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,918
Vehicles, equipment, facilities: service runs on handovers.

2
00:00:05,138 --> 00:00:08,478
A shift changes, and the technician's finding is lost.

3
00:00:08,698 --> 00:00:12,454
Managers chase answers across notes, calls and systems.

4
00:00:12,674 --> 00:00:16,660
Hours go to asking, searching and re-keying, not doing the work.

5
00:00:16,880 --> 00:00:21,697
So critical issues stay buried until they cause delays, rework or harm.

6
00:00:22,417 --> 00:00:25,750
Here is the solution, powered by Deloitte and NVIDIA.

7
00:00:26,470 --> 00:00:29,298
This is where the Service Operations Agent comes in.

8
00:00:29,518 --> 00:00:33,323
One live view of every job, shown in automotive service.

9
00:00:33,543 --> 00:00:37,391
Right now, 12 vehicles are flagged as unsafe to release.

10
00:00:38,411 --> 00:00:42,305
Here is how it works. A technician speaks or types an update.

11
00:00:42,525 --> 00:00:46,745
NVIDIA Riva transcribes it, and Nemotron extracts the facts.

12
00:00:46,965 --> 00:00:50,256
Code verifies every fact. Nothing is guessed.

13
00:00:50,476 --> 00:00:52,515
Each update joins an audit trail.

14
00:00:52,735 --> 00:00:55,886
Managers simply ask, and receive cited answers.

15
00:00:56,906 --> 00:01:00,572
Let us follow one update. A technician dictates it from the bay.

16
00:01:00,792 --> 00:01:03,430
NVIDIA Riva turns the speech into text.

17
00:01:03,650 --> 00:01:07,641
Nemotron extracts the facts: the measurement and the spec.

18
00:01:08,461 --> 00:01:13,193
Code verifies it and flags the repair order unsafe to release, instantly.

19
00:01:14,513 --> 00:01:17,204
A manager now asks the question that matters.

20
00:01:17,424 --> 00:01:20,298
Which vehicles cannot be released on safety grounds?

21
00:01:20,518 --> 00:01:25,389
13 vehicles, each one cited, in a tenth of a second.

22
00:01:26,009 --> 00:01:30,365
An open question: has anyone seen a whistling noise on a Passat?

23
00:01:30,585 --> 00:01:35,402
Search, reranking and a cited answer, in seconds, on one GPU.

24
00:01:36,622 --> 00:01:40,193
Business impact: unsafe vehicles surface immediately.

25
00:01:40,413 --> 00:01:42,868
Managers get answers in a tenth of a second.

26
00:01:43,088 --> 00:01:47,123
Every figure traces to a real record, and one update feeds it all.

27
00:01:47,843 --> 00:01:53,413
Behind it, the architecture: three NVIDIA NIMs on one L40S.

28
00:01:54,033 --> 00:01:58,488
Riva handles speech. NeMo Guardrails stops unsafe requests.

29
00:01:58,708 --> 00:02:02,698
NeMo Evaluator scores every release. That is the whole stack.

30
00:02:03,918 --> 00:02:09,023
It is all observable: DCGM and app metrics, live in Grafana.

31
00:02:10,043 --> 00:02:15,890
In summary: safety first. Unsafe vehicles are flagged as updates are logged.

32
00:02:16,110 --> 00:02:20,744
Answers in a tenth of a second, traced to records, on one GPU you own.

33
00:02:20,964 --> 00:02:26,348
Fast. Grounded. Yours to run. Shown in automotive, built for service operations.

